  "callerScope": {
    "_comment": [
      "Who is asking decides what a request may do. Rust learns the caller from the peer PID: it walks the",
      "parent chain and returns the first running IDE agent it meets, with that agent's role. No agent in the",
      "chain: external. A supervisor: supervisor. Any other agent: worker, refused at admission. A PID that",
      "cannot be read is refused like a worker (fail closed). Scope checks run in the dispatcher, after the",
      "request has parsed, so an unparseable request is still invalid_request / invalid_params first."
    ],
    "callers": {
      "external": {
        "methods": [
          "list_agents",
          "read_output",
          "send_input",
          "kill",
          "spawn",
          "list_projects",
          "await_result",
          "remove_worktree"
        ],
        "scope": "all_agents",
        "mayPass": ["role", "permissionMode"]
      },
      "supervisor": {
        "methods": [
          "list_projects",
          "list_agents",
          "read_output",
          "await_result",
          "send_input",
          "spawn",
          "kill",
          "remove_worktree"
        ],
        "scope": "own_children",
        "outsideScope": "unknown_agent",
        "refusedParams": {
          "role": "invalid_params",
          "permissionMode": "outside_supervisor_scope"
        },
        "requiredSpawnParams": ["provider", "model", "headless"],
        "listProjects": "allowed_only_with_supervisor_block",
        "spawnPolicy": "supervisorPolicy.fixtures.json checkSpawn; refusal is supervisor_denied with its reason",
        "children": {
          "role": "worker",
          "spawnedByAgentId": "<the supervisor's agent id>",
          "runSource": "supervisor"
        },
        "worktrees": "spawn may pass worktree: true; remove_worktree removes an own child's worktree only when it holds no uncommitted change and no unmerged commit, otherwise answers removed: false and leaves it for a person. No path and no force are accepted: the folder is the child's own working directory.",
        "typing": "send_input reaches its own interactive children only, like read_output and kill. It can answer a child's question or permission prompt, so the launch prompt tells the supervisor which ones it may answer and which go to the human. A headless child still refuses it (headless_no_stdin)."
      },
      "worker": {
        "methods": [],
        "admission": "forbidden_agent_caller"
      }
    },
    "cases": [
